Package: scf
Title: Tools for Analyzing the Survey of Consumer Finances
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Joseph", "Cohen", , "joseph.cohen@qc.cuny.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(affiliation = "Department of Sociology, CUNY Queens College"))
Description: A suite of functions to support of the U.S. Federal
    Reserve's 'Survey of Consumer Finances' (SCF) public-use microdata. 
    It wraps the SCF's multiply-imputed, replicate-weighted data into a custom 
    object class ('scf_mi_survey') and supports the estimation of population-level
    statistics from that object, including univariate and bivariate
    variable distributions, hypothesis testing, data visualization, and
    basic regression modeling. The package is designed to make the SCF's
    public-use microdata accessible to analysts who are familiar with
    general statistical methods but have not yet specialized in the
    analysis of multiply- imputed or complex survey data. All functions
    emphasize transparency, reproducibility, and pedagogical clarity to
    facilitate diagnostics, exploration, and learning.
